.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt TCC 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm tcc ,
.Nm cc
.Nd Tiny C Compiler
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm tcc
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar file ...
.Nm cc
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is TinyCC 0.9.27, installed as a static i386 executable.
It includes an assembler and a linker; the machine has no binutils.
It compiles C89 with the C99 features implemented by TinyCC.
The C library is musl.
.Pp
The assembler reads the syntax of GNU as.
The directives
.Ic .code16
and
.Ic .code32 ,
and on x86-64
.Ic .code64 ,
select the size of the code that follows, and a file begins in the
machine's own; 16-bit code addresses memory through
.Li %bx ,
.Li %bp ,
.Li %si
and
.Li %di .
A label less an earlier label of its section is right in any field, the
first defined before the difference or after it; the earlier label less a
later one is an error until the later is defined.
Neither a forward
.Ic loop
or
.Ic jecxz
nor a forward jump is shortened: the first is an error and the second takes
the long form.
.Pp
Executables must be linked with
.Fl static
and must use ELF format: the C library is here only as a static archive,
with no loader for a dynamic program.
Running compiled code from memory with
.Fl run
and producing shared libraries with
.Fl shared
are errors.
Bounds checking with
.Fl b
is not built because musl lacks the required hooks.
.Pp
The system header search order is
.Pa /lib/tcc/include ,
then
.Pa /include .
The compiler searches
.Pa /lib/tcc
for its runtime archive and
.Pa /lib
for the C library and startup objects.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Ss General options
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c
Generate an object file.
.It Fl o Ar file
Write the output to
.Ar file .
.It Fl run Ar source Op Ar args ...
Request compilation and execution from memory.
This is an error on Rach2.
.It Fl v
Print the compiler version.
.It Fl vv
Show included files.
Used alone, print search directories.
.Fl vvv
also shows files tried during the search.
.It Fl bench
Print compilation statistics.
.El
.Ss Preprocessor options
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl I Ar dir
Add a header search directory.
Directories are searched in the order given, before the system directories.
.It Fl D Ar sym Ns Op = Ns Ar val
Define a preprocessor symbol.
The value defaults to 1.
Function-like macros may also be defined, as in
.Ql -DF(a)=a+1 .
.It Fl U Ar sym
Undefine a preprocessor symbol.
.It Fl E
Preprocess only.
Write to standard output, or to the file selected by
.Fl o .
.El
.Ss Compilation options
The following
.Fl f
options have negative forms beginning with
.Ql -fno- .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl funsigned-char
Make plain
.Vt char
unsigned.
.It Fl fsigned-char
Make plain
.Vt char
signed.
.It Fl fno-common
Do not generate common symbols for uninitialized data.
.It Fl fleading-underscore
Prefix C symbols with an underscore.
.It Fl fms-extensions
Treat a nested named structure declaration without an identifier as an
unnamed structure.
.It Fl fdollars-in-identifiers
Allow dollar signs in identifiers.
.It Fl O Ns Op Ar level
Does not select an optimization level; a positive numeric level defines
.Dv __OPTIMIZE__
as 1.
Unsupported GCC
.Fl f
and
.Fl m
options are also ignored.
.El
.Ss Warning options
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl w
Disable all warnings.
.It Fl Wimplicit-function-declaration
Warn about implicit function declarations.
.It Fl Wunsupported
Warn about unsupported GCC features that the compiler ignores.
.It Fl Wwrite-strings
Give string constants type
.Vt const char *
instead of
.Vt char * .
.It Fl Werror
Stop compilation if warnings are issued.
.It Fl Wall
Enable all warnings except
.Fl Werror ,
.Fl Wunsupported ,
.Fl Wgcc-compat
and
.Fl Wwrite-strings .
.El
.Pp
The
.Fl W
options have negative forms beginning with
.Ql -Wno- .
.Ss Linker options
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl L Ar dir
Add a library search directory for
.Fl l .
.It Fl l Ar lib
Link with the library
.Pa lib Ns Ar lib Ns Pa .a
for a static link.
Directories given by
.Fl L
are searched before those in
.Ev LIBRARY_PATH .
.It Fl B Ar dir
Set the directory of the compiler's runtime archive.
The default is
.Pa /lib/tcc ;
the header paths stay
.Pa /lib/tcc/include
and
.Pa /include .
.It Fl static
Link a static executable.
Required for an executable on Rach2.
.It Fl shared
Request a shared library.
This is an error on Rach2.
.It Fl soname Ar name
Set a shared library's runtime name.
Shared-library output is unavailable on Rach2.
.It Fl rdynamic
Export global symbols to a dynamic loader.
Executables are static here, and no loader reads them.
.It Fl r
Combine the input files into one object file.
.It Fl Wl, Ns Ar option Ns Op , Ns Ar option ...
Pass options to the linker, as listed below.
.El
.Pp
Linker options include:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl Wl,-rpath= Ns Ar path
Record a search path for dynamic libraries.
The static output carries no
.Dv DT_RPATH .
.It Fl Wl,--enable-new-dtags
Use
.Dv DT_RUNPATH
instead of
.Dv DT_RPATH
for a dynamic-library search path; the static output carries neither.
.It Fl Wl,--oformat= Ns Ar format
Select the output format.
The default is
.Ql elf32-i386 .
Non-ELF executable output, including
.Ql binary ,
is refused on Rach2.
The upstream
.Ql coff
format is for the TMS320C67xx target only.
.It Fl Wl,-Ttext= Ns Ar address
Set the text address in the executable layout.
.It Fl Wl,-T,\& Ns Ar script , Fl Wl,--script= Ns Ar script
Lay a static executable out by the GNU ld script in the file
.Ar script :
the addresses and load addresses of its sections, its program headers,
which the script must name in
.Ic PHDRS ,
and the symbols it assigns.
The script may have
.Ic ENTRY ,
assignments,
.Ic PHDRS ,
and
.Ic SECTIONS
with
.Ic AT ,
input section patterns and
.Pa /DISCARD/ ;
its expressions may have
.Ic ALIGN ,
.Ic ADDR ,
.Ic LOADADDR ,
.Ic SIZEOF
and
.Ic SIZEOF_HEADERS .
Anything else is an error.
The x86-64 kernel is linked so on Rach2.
.It Fl Wl,-section-alignment= Ns Ar value
Set section alignment in the executable layout: with a script, the
alignment modulo which a segment's file offset follows its address.
.It Fl Wl,-file-alignment= Ns Ar value
An option of the Windows target; the Rach2 compiler rejects it as an
unsupported linker option.
.It Fl Wl,-image-base= Ns Ar address
Set the image base in the executable layout.
.It Fl Wl,-stack= Ns Ar size
An option of the Windows target; the Rach2 compiler rejects it as an
unsupported linker option.
.It Fl Wl,-subsystem= Ns Ar subsystem
Select a subsystem for PE executables, such as
.Ql console ,
.Ql gui
or
.Ql wince .
This is an option for the Windows target.
.It Fl Wl,-Bsymbolic
Set the
.Dv DT_SYMBOLIC
tag, which the static output does not carry.
.It Fl Wl,-whole-archive
Link every object in archives.
.It Fl Wl,-no-whole-archive
Turn off linking every object in archives.
.El
.Ss Debugging options
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl g
Generate debugging information.
.It Fl b
Request allocation and array or pointer bounds checks.
This option is not built on Rach2.
.It Fl bt Ar n
Set the number of callers displayed in stack traces during execution from
memory, which Rach2 rejects; the option has no effect on file output.
.El
.Ss Other options
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl MD
Generate a makefile fragment containing dependencies.
.It Fl MF Ar file
Write the dependencies from
.Fl MD
to
.Ar file .
.It Fl print-search-dirs
Print the configured installation, library and include directories.
.It Fl dumpversion
Print the compiler version.
.It Fl mms-bitfields
Use MSVC bit-field alignment instead of GCC alignment.
.It Fl mfloat-abi Ar abi
Select
.Ql softfp
or
.Ql hard
floating-point ABI on the ARM target.
.It Fl mno-sse
Disable SSE registers on the x86_64 target.
.It Fl m32
Continue with this i386 compiler.
.It Fl m64
Run
.Nm x86_64-tcc ,
which the images do not install.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /lib/tcc/libtcc1.a
.It Pa /bin/tcc , /bin/cc
Two regular files containing the same compiler bytes.
KRFFS has no symbolic links.
.It Pa /lib/tcc/include
The compiler's five headers.
.It Pa /include
The musl headers.
.It Pa /lib/tcc/libtcc1.a
The compiler runtime archive.
.It Pa /lib/libc.a
The musl C library.
.It Pa /lib/crt1.o , /lib/crti.o , /lib/crtn.o
Startup objects.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl tcc -static -o hello hello.c && ./hello
.Pp
In the source tree,
.Ql tests/run tcc
compiles and runs a program on os-real.
.Ql tests/run selfbuild
builds the kernel through
.Xr make 1 .
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
The output-policy errors are:
.Bl -item
.It
.Ql -run is not available on Rach2: this tcc is a static program, so code it runs from memory cannot reach the C library. Compile to a file and run that.
.It
.Ql -shared is not available on Rach2: this tcc's C library, musl, is here only as a static archive, and nothing loads a shared object built against it.
.It
.Ql a program for Rach2 must be linked with -static: this tcc's C library, musl, is here only as a static archive, with no loader for a dynamic program.
.It
.Ql a program for Rach2 must be an ELF: -Wl,-oformat asks for a raw image, and exec reads a program header table.
.El
.Pp
The unavailable
.Fl b
option produces
.Ql invalid option -- '-b' .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr make 1 ,
.Xr rach2 7
